  "raw_response": "{\n  \"title\": \"US 100 short entry using Fibonacci retracement after DeepSeek-driven breakdown\",\n  \"school\": \"Price Action\",\n  \"asset\": \"US 100 Cash CFD\",\n  \"timeframe\": \"1H\",\n  \"market_context\": \"After a sharp selloff triggered by DeepSeek news (≈6% drop), price broke prior structure downward. The analyst applied the reverse of the long setup: measuring the bearish impulse move that broke structure, then waiting for retracement to the Fibonacci gold zone for a short entry.\",\n  \"key_observation\": \"The analyst identified the bearish impulse move that broke previous structure (top to bottom of the strong down-candle cluster), drew Fibonacci retracement from that swing high to low, and noted price retracing into the 0.5–0.618 'gold zone' as the optimal short entry zone.\",\n  \"analysis_steps\": [\n    \"Step 1: Identify the bearish impulse move that broke the previous structure — specifically the strongest consecutive bearish candles with no pullbacks, including the wick, from swing high to swing low.\",\n    \"Step 2: Draw Fibonacci retracement from the top (swing high) to the bottom (swing low) of that impulse move.\",\n    \"Step 3: Wait for price to retrace into the Fibonacci gold zone (0.5 to 0.618 level), where selling weakness and rejection patterns (e.g., bearish engulfing, doji) confirm entry.\",\n    \"Step 4: Enter short at the gold zone, with take-profit targeting the prior swing low (previous structure low), not Fibonacci extensions, for safer risk management.\"\n  ],\n  \"outcome\": \"T",
